(4. Main Data Entities) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(sku_rules: the category and sub-category rule table used to build valid SKUs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(sku_catalog: the SKU master table that stores item identity and warehouse metadata such as) Tj
T*
(part name, part number, dimensions, weight, storage, rack, bin, family, image, and comments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(barcode_log: the generated QR history table. Each row stores SKU, year, quarter, serial) Tj
T*
(number, barcode value, and timestamps. Deletes are soft deletes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(barcode_serials: a tracker table that stores the last used serial for each SKU and period) Tj
T*
(combination.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(app_users and app_roles: authentication and authorization tables for login, role policy, and) Tj
T*
(optional per-user permission override.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(app_audit_log: records sensitive actions, denials, edits, deletes, and other traceable) Tj
T*
(events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(app_meta and app_backup_history: store application metadata and automated backup history.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Startup Workflow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. The application starts in src/main.cpp and opens MainWindow.) Tj
T*
(2. MainWindow builds the UI, menu actions, and signal wiring.) Tj
T*
(3. The app selects or opens the SQLite database path.) Tj
T*
(4. If the database is available, the app ensures schema, default roles, seed data, and) Tj
T*
(embedded admin availability.) Tj
T*
(5. The app prompts for login.) Tj
T*
(6. After successful login, it loads category rules, SKU lists, history filters, dashboard) Tj
T*
(metrics, and backup scheduling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If startup database selection is skipped, the window can remain in a no-database state until) Tj
T*
(the user loads a database later.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. SKU Workflow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The SKU workflow begins in the SKU Generation tab.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Users choose a category and sub-category that come from the seeded SKU rules. They then) Tj
T*
(enter item details such as part name, part number, weight, storage information, rack and bin) Tj
T*
(location, product family, comments, and optionally an image.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The app computes the SKU from business rule components:) Tj
T*
(category digit + sub-category digit + item serial padded to 3 digits + variation code) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Variation codes use digits first and then letters for higher values. The app blocks invalid) Tj
T*
(or duplicate SKU creation.) Tj
ET
